<section class="box-exercise">
<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Organic_Chemistry/Organic_Chemistry_(Morsch_et_al.)/25:_Biomolecules-_Carbohydrates/25.04:_Configurations_of_Aldoses" class="mt-section"><span id="Exercise_.5C(.5CPageIndex.7B2.7D.5C)"></span><h5 class="box-legend editable"><span class="lt-icon-default">Exercise \(\PageIndex{2}\)</span></h5>

<p>How many heptose stereoisomers would there expected to be? How many would be D-Sugars?</p>

<dl>
    <dt><strong class="emphasis bold">Answer</strong></dt>
    <dd>
    <p>There would be 2<sup>5</sup> = 32 heptose stereoisomers. Half of these would be D-sugars or 16.</p>
    </dd>
</dl>
